---
import PluginsLayout from '../../layouts/PluginsLayout.astro';
import {site} from '../../config/site.mjs';
import {publishedPlugins} from '../../config/plugins.mjs';
export function getStaticPaths(){return site.template==='client'?[]:[{params:{catalog:undefined}}];}
---
<PluginsLayout title="Plugins | EZERWRIGHT" description="Explore the EZERWRIGHT plugin catalog in preparation, learn what future listings will include, and discuss separately scoped integrations.">
  <section class="container plugin-hero">
    <div><h1>Useful tools.<br/><span>Thoughtfully connected.</span></h1><p class="plugin-lead">A home for EZERWRIGHT plugins and connectors. Small additions with a clear purpose, helping your tools work better together.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="#catalog">Explore the catalog <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><a class="text-link" href="/plugins/services/">Discuss an integration <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div>
    <aside class="plugin-principle" aria-label="Our approach to plugins"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 320 130" fill="none"><path d="M52 65h79m58 0h79" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/><rect x="10" y="30" width="68" height="70" rx="12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/><rect x="126" y="12" width="68" height="106" rx="12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/><rect x="242" y="30" width="68" height="70" rx="12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/><path d="m145 65 10 10 20-22" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/></svg><p>One useful connection.<br/>A clearer way to work.</p><small>A considered approach to extending your tools.</small></aside>
  </section>
  <section class="plugin-catalog" id="catalog" aria-labelledby="catalog-title"><div class="container">
    <div class="plugin-section-heading"><h2 id="catalog-title">The catalog</h2><p>Purpose before possibility.</p></div>
    {publishedPlugins.length ? <div class="plugin-list">{publishedPlugins.map(plugin=><article><p class="small-copy">{plugin.platforms.join(' · ')}</p><h3><a href={`/plugins/${plugin.slug}/`}>{plugin.name}</a></h3><p>{plugin.summary}</p><a class="text-link" href={`/plugins/${plugin.slug}/`}>View plugin <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article>)}</div> : <div class="plugin-empty"><span class="plugin-status">Catalog in preparation</span><h3>Good tools take considered work.</h3><p>There are no published plugins yet. When a plugin is ready, you’ll find its purpose, requirements, permissions and installation guidance here.</p><a class="text-link" href="/plugins/services/">Have a connection in mind? <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>}
  </div></section>
  <section class="container plugin-explainer" aria-labelledby="connection-title"><div><h2 id="connection-title">Know what you’re connecting.</h2><p>Plugins extend a host application. Connectors link tools or data. MCP (Model Context Protocol) is one way an AI application can access tools and context.</p><p>Each ecosystem has its own installation process and permission model. A connection should fit the task—and the access you’re comfortable granting.</p></div><dl class="plugin-disclosures"><div><dt>Fit comes first</dt><dd>Future listings will identify supported platforms and prerequisites. Compatibility is specific to each release.</dd></div><div><dt>Access should be clear</dt><dd>Permissions and data practices belong beside the installation steps, where you can review them.</dd></div><div><dt>A useful handover</dt><dd>Documentation, source, license and version details will help you understand what you’re installing.</dd></div></dl></section>
  <section class="container plugin-next"><div><h2>Need help connecting the pieces?</h2><p>Discuss installation, a custom connector or a review of an existing setup. Scope and support are agreed separately.</p></div><a class="button" href="/plugins/services/">Explore integration services <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></section>
  <div class="container plugin-crosslinks"><p>Building your business website? <a href="/services/">Explore the existing $500 website package.</a></p><a href="/contact/">Contact EZERWRIGHT</a></div>
</PluginsLayout>
